  "worked_solution": "First, we recall the following:\n\n- If ${h}^{′}(t)=0$ for all $t\\in (a,b),$ then $h(t)$ is constant on $(a,b).$\n\n- When ${h}^{′}(t)>0$ for all $t\\in (a,b),$ then $h(t)$ is increasing on $(a,b).$\n\n- When ${h}^{′}(t)<0$ for all $t\\in (a,b),$ then $h(t)$ is decreasing on $(a,b).$\n\nFrom the above graph, we can see that ${h}^{′}(t)$ is positive on the intervals $[0,3)$ and $(6,9]:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14193353/assets/35b4ea0dc5200e0ed009b00320a88927daadd65265f245d7624edb95f57d8712.png)\n\nTherefore, the price of a burger is increasing when $t\\in [0,3)\\cup (6,9].$",
